{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1367204-upcoming-books","id":1367204,"title":"Upcoming Books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-12T06:34:11-08:00","id":1367204,"title":"Upcoming Books?","content":"With the release of Shunned by the Moon, I haven't heard much about upcoming WtF books in production. Indeed, I've heard only about VtR and MtAw books (beyond the core and Kickstarter stretch goals for CtL and beyond)<br /> <br /> Is that it for Forsaken for a while, or are there other books in production I am unaware of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T09:46:49-08:00","id":1367244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1367204-upcoming-books#post1367204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the release of Shunned by the Moon, I haven't heard much about upcoming WtF books in production. Indeed, I've heard only about VtR and MtAw books (beyond the core and Kickstarter stretch goals for CtL and beyond)<br /> <br /> Is that it for Forsaken for a while, or are there other books in production I am unaware of?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last Vampire the Requiem (on the production list) is coming out today. And the only Awakening thing on the list is in layout.<br /> <br /> We don't know. Hopefully there's more, they used to announce these things in batches at cons but we haven't heard anything about any of the Chronicles games in the past couple. It doesn't seem like anything's been cancelled, things have just not been announced or started on yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2020, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:42:02-08:00","id":1367531,"title":"","content":"I am actually kind of curious about the future of this. While I don't fully grasp the lore very well and I have no idea if I like or not the mechanics the concept is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T08:30:10-08:00","id":1367541,"title":"","content":"There's nothing on the MMN, but that doesn't mean there are no plans. Tome of the Pentacle (MtAw) is nowhere in the notes but it's been confirmed in progress since like 2017 I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 02-13-2020, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T08:47:30-08:00","id":1367544,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25136_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25136\" data-vbnamecard=\"25136\">Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</a> I'm the opposite. I don't always fully grasp the mechanics, but the lore part is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:12:08-08:00","id":1367549,"title":"","content":"Only playtime can solve such dilemmas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T11:08:43-08:00","id":1367567,"title":"","content":"Totally true! lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T12:54:08-08:00","id":1367583,"title":"","content":"I forget: was &quot;Secrets of the Tribes&quot; cancelled or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T16:22:37-08:00","id":1367640,"title":"","content":"As far as I know it never appeared beyond that one (possibly more) brochure and no one's mentioned it, but apparently stuff being worked on isn't usually mentioned until it's officially announced. Which I guess the brochure could count as an official announcement but no one's said anything about working on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T17:36:58-08:00","id":1367652,"title":"","content":"I definitely could use a lot more insight into the 2E Storm Lords in particular, as the intersection of their role with their favored prey never clicked for me, and has always left them feeling like the odd one\u2019s out. So I hope Secrets of the Tribes sees the light of day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T02:37:12-08:00","id":1367713,"title":"","content":"I felt a bit cold with the tribes (cults?) as I remember them from the core book, unlike Courts or Covenants, so I hope that's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T13:04:39-08:00","id":1368103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1367204-upcoming-books?p=1367652#post1367652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely could use a lot more insight into the 2E Storm Lords in particular, as the intersection of their role with their favored prey never clicked for me, and has always left them feeling like the odd one\u2019s out. So I hope Secrets of the Tribes sees the light of day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always interpreted them as insulating themselves from their loved ones and followers in such a way that when/if someone is possessed, the pack is less vulnerable, as its leadership hasn't allowed the now suborned member to see weakness. It requires assuming that the Ridden are a regular enough &quot;enemy within&quot; style threat, where the people close to the pack are the ones most likely to be possessed. That way the tribe oath makes a kind of sense as an internal security/compartmentalization sort of deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:08:33-08:00","id":1368283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1367204-upcoming-books?p=1368103#post1368103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always interpreted them as insulating themselves from their loved ones and followers in such a way that when/if someone is possessed, the pack is less vulnerable, as its leadership hasn't allowed the now suborned member to see weakness. It requires assuming that the Ridden are a regular enough &quot;enemy within&quot; style threat, where the people close to the pack are the ones most likely to be possessed. That way the tribe oath makes a kind of sense as an internal security/compartmentalization sort of deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's really an interesting idea, but as you said it requires Ridden to be targeting the pack which doesn't make much sense. It's a whole lotta risk for no more gain than riding any other human. The spirit would have a specific reason to target the pack or that pack member, and I can't come up with any where my go-to solution would be Fetter, Possess, or Claim. Well, possibly Claim because you could force them to have to kill a pack member, but then the spirit would have to deal with having their host destroyed and quite probably be ejected in front of the whole hunting party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T13:29:39-08:00","id":1369001,"title":"","content":"personally, I feel the storm lord sacred prey makes sense, but still should be elaborated on. because unlike every other sacred prey, you have to kill it twice. specifically talking about the Claimed here. that, to me, means they should at least have more on how they treat spirits in general and their knowledge on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T14:54:56-08:00","id":1369028,"title":"","content":"Can always imprison them forever via bane and ban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T14:20:50-08:00","id":1370444,"title":"","content":"If I can chime in with my $0.02. The Claimed make more sense when you compare them to the Strix in Vampire. If you read the Strix chronicles fiction, every story is about how Vampires get mysteriously possessed by one of the Owls, which leads to them wrecking havoc on a domain and increase the level of paranoia. When anyone, including yourself, can be the enemy, then suddenly the Claimed become really scary and the claim that the Claimed are the most dangerous prey can actually make sense.<br /> <br /> The same goes with Mage. In the Fall of the Exarchs, there are numerous examples of people being controlled by the Exarchs or Seers and either spying or being used against the mages. Heck, the Profane Urim is a tool to control those closest to Mages and use them. In the beginner adventure Gloria Mundi, there are numerous scenes where a Mage, including the player characters, can get possessed by a Spirit.<br /> <br /> So yea, when your family and packmates get possessed by a Spirit it can be pretty scary. I wondered if Werewolves can get possessed, but since the rules state that the victim gets to roll attribute plus Primal Urge, I take that as a yes. This is one enemy that claws and fang alone cannot always beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}